  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given infinite series is $\\frac{1^{2}+2^{2}}{3 !}+\\frac{1^{2}+2^{2}+3^{2}}{4 !}$\r\n$\\begin{aligned} \\frac{1^{2}+2^{2}}{3 !} &+\\frac{1^{2}+2^{2}+3^{2}}{4 !} \\\\ &+\\frac{1^{2}+2^{2}+3^{2}+4^{2}}{5 !}+\\ldots \\end{aligned}$\r\nnth term, $t_{n}=\\frac{1^{2}+2^{2}+3^{2}+4^{2}+\\ldots+(r+1)^{2}}{(r+2) !}$\r\nNow, $S_{n}=\\Sigma t_{n}=\\sum_{r=1}^{n} \\frac{1^{2}+2^{2}+3^{2}+\\ldots+(r+1)^{2}}{(r+2) !}$\r\n$=\\sum_{r=1}^{n} \\frac{(r+1)(r+2)(2 n+3)}{6(r+2) !}$\r\n$\\left[\\because \\Sigma n^{2}=\\frac{n(n+1)(2 n+1)}{6}\\right]$\r\n$=\\sum_{r=1}^{n} \\frac{(2 r+3)}{6 \\cdot r !}=\\frac{1}{6} \\sum_{r=1}^{n}\\left\\{\\frac{2}{(r-1) !}+\\frac{3}{r !}\\right\\}$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{6}\\left\\{\\left(\\frac{2}{1}+\\frac{3}{1 !}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{2}{1 !}+\\frac{3}{2 !}\\right)+\\left(\\frac{2}{2 !}+\\frac{3}{3 !}\\right)+\\ldots\\right\\}$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{6}\\left\\{\\left(\\frac{2}{1 !}+\\frac{2}{1 !}+\\frac{2}{2 !}+\\ldots\\right)+\\left(\\frac{3}{1 !}+\\frac{3}{2 !}+\\frac{3}{3 !}+\\ldots\\right)\\right\\}$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{6}\\left\\{2\\left(1+\\frac{1}{1 !}+\\frac{1}{2 !}+\\ldots\\right)+3\\left(\\frac{1}{1 !}+\\frac{1}{2 !}+\\ldots\\right)\\right\\}$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{6}\\{2 e+3(e-1)\\}$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{6}\\{2 e+3 e-3\\}$\r\n$=\\frac{1}{6}(5 e-3)=\\frac{5 e}{6}-\\frac{1}{2}$",
    "image": null
  },
